{"id": "EUVD-2026-55391", "enisaUuid": "2da6ada8-a712-33e1-8f26-f8f8d86d02eb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrds: tcp: unregister sysctl before tearing down listen socket\n\nrds_tcp_exit_net() frees the per-netns RDS TCP listen socket via\nrds_tcp_kill_sock() before unregistering the per-netns sysctl table.  Since\nrds_tcp_skbuf_handler() derives the netns from\nrtn->rds_tcp_listen_sock->sk, a concurrent sysctl write can race with\nnetns teardown and dereference the freed socket/sk.\n\nKASAN reports the race as:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in rds_tcp_skbuf_handler+0x2aa/0x2e0\n  rds_tcp_skbuf_handler              net/rds/tcp.c:721\n  proc_sys_call_handler              fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c\n  vfs_write                          fs/read_write.c\n  __x64_sys_pwrite64                 fs/read_write.c\n\nFix this by unregistering the RDS TCP sysctl table before calling\nrds_tcp_kill_sock().  unregister_net_sysctl_table() prevents new sysctl\nhandlers from starting and waits for in-flight handlers to finish, so\nthe listen socket can then be released safely. The fix was tested\nagainst the linked reproducer.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:02:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:43", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80fffed08dc1c10e971066941d2daa56253f1552", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16df2d154ec82e2f7e7585b4fa154751ba37729a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3aa13fe0c1bb7bc5312f878e61523e5d8cf3f85d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/167e54c703ccd4fa028feb568b0d1002020cff86"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j86x-f498-4jqp", "CVE-2026-68290"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0128a327-e4df-33dd-a06e-45b81ff55e21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "0d9e2738-a018-34e4-863d-ac3810dc038e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f5611cbc4871c7fb1ad36c2e5a9edad63dca95c <16df2d154ec82e2f7e7585b4fa154751ba37729a"}, {"id": "28a4d6f4-32b5-3d8b-8d1b-0d6467a588d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "2dfac956-c017-3aeb-8615-8390ae7a6aad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f5611cbc4871c7fb1ad36c2e5a9edad63dca95c <167e54c703ccd4fa028feb568b0d1002020cff86"}, {"id": "497974b7-e009-3619-937a-d10dc17030ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "4a6c2b63-1627-39eb-aae5-c8426c7a6f6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "731cf67a-d4be-3448-8511-48ac23617cf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f5611cbc4871c7fb1ad36c2e5a9edad63dca95c <3aa13fe0c1bb7bc5312f878e61523e5d8cf3f85d"}, {"id": "7526e1dc-7e98-35c9-b0e1-d61629e7822c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a690f611-1f67-3f2e-aad4-2c4e4f3510c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.160 <6.7"}, {"id": "b77a282e-86bc-3f9e-ace2-cb9c9e4e1946", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.10 <6.12.101"}, {"id": "c4e6d438-ac34-3c53-a6da-22b13384a541", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "33b3e09a489a31b30342b77cc55290f025d95c7e"}, {"id": "d83e48dd-d832-347a-b5ae-c052f9cc05ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de8d6de0ee27be4b2b1e5b06f04aeacbabbba492 <80fffed08dc1c10e971066941d2daa56253f1552"}, {"id": "f47cd27f-7757-3b2f-9e03-8488049e952a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "88a6a9c2-d6a0-383b